# v1 (superseded) — kept for the record of what was cut and why

The original 24-phase draft below aimed at the full distributed-systems
tech tree (Kafka with 6 event types, Redis with stampede/penetration/
avalanche mitigation, full OAuth stack, S3, Elasticsearch, CQRS, Saga,
sharding, canary deploys, circuit breakers, bulkheads) for a project with
no real production traffic. Two things from it were genuinely good and
were pulled into v2 above rather than discarded: **Phase 22** ("never
invent metrics, measure everything" — now `docs/benchmarks.md`) and
**Phase 23** (the production-mindset checklist — can this survive a
DB/cache/broker outage, no-downtime deploys — worth reasoning through in
the README even for pieces not built). Everything else is preserved
as-is below purely as a record, not a plan to execute.

# Baaki - Implementation Master Plan (Resume-Grade Backend Project)

> Goal: Build a production-grade expense sharing platform that demonstrates backend engineering skills expected by top product companies (Amazon, Microsoft, Google, Uber, Atlassian, Walmart, Salesforce, etc.) in the AI era.

---

# Vision

Baaki is **NOT** a Splitwise clone.

Baaki is a backend engineering showcase.

Every feature should exist because it demonstrates an engineering concept:

- scalability
- concurrency
- reliability
- performance
- security
- distributed systems
- production readiness

The objective is that an interviewer can spend **45-60 minutes** discussing this single project.

